   "subject": "Volcano plots for Log2FC of Inf and -Inf values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">When using MSstats to process DDA data you often get missing values in one condition or another that result in Log2FC of Inf, -Inf, or NA.  When plotting such volcano plots, you end up with a bunch of dots up in the corners.  I think it would be great to have an option in the volcano plots to exclude proteins for a given comparision plot for which the Log2FC is Inf, -Inf, or NA.<div><br></div><div>-Danielle</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "BajmUYfYCAAJ",
   "from": "Meena Choi",
   "author": "df9ba0266a9a081f",
   "date": "2017-07-18T19:40:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: Volcano plots for Log2FC of Inf and -Inf values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Here is temporary solution. You can filter out the testing result with any issue before drawing volcano plot.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">test </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groupComparison</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">contrast</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">comparison</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">QuantData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">test2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> test$ComparisonResult</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test$ComparisonResult$issue</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">groupComparisonPlots</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;VolcanoPlot&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></div></code></div><div><br></div>Hope to help.</div><div>- Meena<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
